    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107901" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρτον-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strained to the utmost, at
				full pitch, exceeding loud,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γήρυμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					569
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1154
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				46
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναμις ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Fab.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τῷ κόπῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hippiatr.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρτονον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύλον</span>), τό,
				<i>main-beam,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				576.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				249.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				780.28
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτονος.</span>)</div>
